026 to 165bp. Norvane still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably (utility-credit).\n- **Equity is the weak spot.** Two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after investor demand fell short (pellham-offering).\n- **Pellham is the constrained case.**\n  - Its 2027 capex is planned up 18%, against 12% for Norvane (utility-capex-2027). Most of it is substations and transformers.\n  - Pellham is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes until financing improves (pellham-offering).\n  - It probably can't close the gap with debt alone, likely because of leverage and credit-rating limits. The sources don't say this directly, so it is my inference.\n- **Norvane looks able to fund its plan mostly with debt.** The sources don't give its equity needs.\n- **Knock-on effect.** Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria (utility-capex-2027), so its cuts will hit transformer and substation suppliers.\n\n**Limits:** I found no data on individual balance sheets, rating headroom or the total size of the funding gap. The Pellham–Norvane split rests on one bond deal and one failed equity raise.\n\nThe two child answers behind this are n7.r1 (debt) and n8.r1 (equity).","ttft_ms":3929,"type":"result","duration_ms":34772,"uuid":"2f51ae4c-6f83-459e-92c5-18c0d5ae7f6f","ttft_stream_ms":3736,"time_to_request_ms":116,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":2,"process_user_input":8,"input_attachments":26,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":16,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":64,"time_to_re